    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1946-10-21">October 21, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4726" type="person">Miss
                        Shearon</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof. Tillich</rs> thanks very
                    much for <rs ref="L11012" type="letter">your letter of Octobre 10</rs>. The
                    review on <rs type="work" ref="#tillich__ASPVVH5A">REVELATION AND REASON</rs> is
                    almost finshed but unfortunately a slight accident at his right hand prevented
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr. Tillich</rs> to do the
                    final job. He will, however, mail it to you within 2–3 days, and I hope it will
                    arrive in time for the next issue.<note type="ea"><rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Tillichs</rs> Rezension
                        erschien im Januar 1947. Vgl. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Paul Tillich</rs>: <rs type="work"
                            ref="#tillich__IVS4G69U">Emil Brunner: Revelation and Reason (1946)</rs>
                        (1947).</note></p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><rs type="person">Secretary to
                            Prof. Tillich</rs></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
